    "sentence-category-reason": "Computes the coordinates of the cube center O.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 10,
    "sentence": "Thus, $A = (0, 0, 0)$, $O = \\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}, \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}, \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$, and $P = \\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}, \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Substitutes a=1/\u221a3 into coordinates for A, O, and P.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 11,
    "sentence": "We want to find the area of triangle $A O P$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "States the goal of finding the area of triangle AOP.",
    "sentence-category": "Read"
  },
  {
    "index": 12,
    "sentence": "We can use the formula $\\frac{1}{2} \\| \\overrightarrow{A O} \\times \\overrightarrow{A P} \\|$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Chooses a method: area via half the norm of the cross product.",
    "sentence-category": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 13,
    "sentence": "$\\overrightarrow{A O} = O - A = \\left(\\frac{a}{2}, \\frac{a}{2}, \\frac{a}{2}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}, \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}, \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Computes the vector AO numerically.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 14,
    "sentence": "$\\overrightarrow{A P} = P - A = \\left(\\frac{a}{2}, \\frac{a}{2}, a\\right) = \\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}, \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Computes the vector AP numerically.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 15,
    "sentence": "$\\overrightarrow{A O} \\times \\overrightarrow{A P} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\frac{a}{2} & \\frac{a}{2} & \\frac{a}{2} \\\\ \\frac{a}{2} & \\frac{a}{2} & a \\end{vmatrix} = \\left(\\frac{a^2}{2} - \\frac{a^2}{4}\\right) \\mathbf{i} - \\left(\\frac{a^2}{2} - \\frac{a^2}{4}\\right) \\mathbf{j} + \\left(\\frac{a^2}{4} - \\frac{a^2}{4}\\right) \\mathbf{k} = \\frac{a^2}{4} \\mathbf{i} - \\frac{a^2}{4} \\mathbf{j} + 0 \\mathbf{k}$\n$\\overrightarrow{A O} \\times \\overrightarrow{A P} = \\left(\\frac{a^2}{4}, -\\frac{a^2}{4}, 0\\right) = \\left(\\frac{1}{12}, -\\frac{1}{12}, 0\\right)$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Calculates the cross product AO \u00d7 AP and simplifies.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 16,
    "sentence": "$\\| \\overrightarrow{A O} \\times \\overrightarrow{A P} \\| = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{a^2}{4}\\right)^2 + \\left(-\\frac{a^2}{4}\\right)^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{a^4}{16} + \\frac{a^4}{16}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{a^4}{8}} = \\frac{a^2}{\\sqrt{8}} = \\frac{a^2}{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})^2}{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{3}}{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{1}{6\\sqrt{2}}$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Computes the magnitude of the cross product to a numeric value.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 17,
    "sentence": "Area of triangle $A O P = \\frac{1}{2} \\| \\overrightarrow{A O} \\times \\overrightarrow{A P} \\| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\frac{1}{6\\sqrt{2}}\\right) = \\frac{1}{12\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{12 \\cdot 2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{24}$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Concludes with the computed area of triangle AOP.",
    "sentence-category": "Answer"
  },
  {
    "index": 18,
    "sentence": "We can calculate the area of the triangle using $\\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{\\| \\overrightarrow{A O} \\|^2 \\| \\overrightarrow{A P} \\|^2 - (\\overrightarrow{A O} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{A P})^2}$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Introduces an alternative formula to compute the area.",
    "sentence-category": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 19,
    "sentence": "$\\| \\overrightarrow{A O} \\| = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{3 a^2}{4}} = \\frac{a \\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2 \\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{1}{2}$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Computes the norm of AO.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 20,
    "sentence": "$\\| \\overrightarrow{A P} \\| = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2 + a^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{a^2}{4} + \\frac{a^2}{4} + a^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{6 a^2}{4}} = \\frac{a \\sqrt{6}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2 \\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Computes the norm of AP.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 21,
    "sentence": "$\\overrightarrow{A O} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{A P} = \\frac{a}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{2} + \\frac{a}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{2} + \\frac{a}{2} \\cdot a = \\frac{a^2}{4} + \\frac{a^2}{4} + \\frac{a^2}{2} = \\frac{a^2}{4} + \\frac{a^2}{4} + \\frac{2 a^2}{4} = a^2 = \\frac{1}{3}$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Performs the dot product calculation and substitutes a^2 = 1/3; concrete computations.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 22,
    "sentence": "Area of triangle $A O P = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^2} = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{2}{4} - \\frac{1}{9}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{8} - \\frac{1}{9}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{9 - 8}{72}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{72}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{72}} = \\frac{1}{2 \\cdot 6 \\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{1}{12 \\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{24}$.",
